> Odd. I'm pretty sure that mummies and zombies should cause food poisoning.

The age of the corpse is divided by d20+9; if the corpse is cursed, 2
is added to this result, if blessed, two subtracted. If the result
is greater than 5, "Ulch, that meat was tainted", and you're liable
to food poisoning; if it's 4 or 5, theres a 4/5 chance of "You feel
sick" and taking d8 damage.

(This is ignoring lizards, lichens, acid blobs, poisonous corpses,
sickness resistance, stoning, various other stuff. Just your average
corpse.)

So, any uncursed corpse 60 turns old or more _may_ give you food
poisoning, 173 turns old or less _may_ not.  Mummy, vampire, and
zombie corpses are started at 100 turns old.

